==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Li'l Gau Gau''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Crystal Li'l Gau Gau''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Li'l Gau is a surprisingly powerful and cheap spammable unit that tanks very well against Dark enemies. Its low range is very helpful as it would allow Li'l Gau to get closer to deadly Dark enemies such as [[Gory Dark]] to help protect the backliners safely from their fast and aggressive attacks. It's simply a better [[Nono (Rare Cat)|Nono]], as it has slightly higher health, lower range, and a lower cost (before Nono's True Form).

==='''True Form'''===
Its True Form gives it more health, now having an HP stat incredibly close to an untalented [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] of the same level, while also having the benefit of being spammable without the need for any Research Up [[Cat Combo|combos]]. This not only improves Gau Gau's mixed stage viability, but also paves the way for it to become a genuinely viable generalist meatshield (ideally with a significant boost to + levels, which should be easy to get duplicates from the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] considering it is only a Rare unit).

Furthermore, Crystal Li'l Gau Gau also gains a minor addition of Immunity to Knockback, which can help in particular against enemies like [[Mr. Mole]], who rely on their Knockback to disorient your frontlines and allow enemy pushers to wipe out your backliners. Overall, Crystal Li'l Gau Gau is an excellent Rare unit to grab. As an added bonus, it doesn't require a lot of resources to evolve the unit, so getting its True Form is very easy and worth it.

{{Job|Classification = Meatshield}}

